   "id": "chelation",
   "num": "4",
   "label": "Metal & Biofilm Cascade",
   "title": "4-Tier Heavy Metal Mobilization, Sulfhydryl Buffering & Luminal Evacuation",
   "summary": "The strict biophysical sequence for mobilizing, chelating, and permanently eliminating toxic heavy metals without redistribution.",
   "html": "<div class=\"card\" data-accent=\"amber\">\n    <h3 class=\"card-kicker\">4.0 The Physics of Safe Heavy Metal Elimination</h3>\n    <p>Eliminating heavy metals without triggering neurotoxicity requires a strict, continuous four-tier biochemical concentration gradient. If metals are mobilized from deep tissues without extracellular chelators and GI binders active, they redistribute directly into brain structures and renal tubules.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"table-scroll\">\n    <table class=\"data\">\n      <thead><tr><th>Drainage Tier</th><th>Primary Therapeutic Agents</th><th>Biophysical &amp; Molecular Mechanism</th><th>Target Compartment</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr><th scope=\"row\" data-accent=\"teal\">Tier 1: Intracellular &amp; CNS Mobilization</th><td><strong>Coriander Tincture</strong> + <strong>Na-R-ALA</strong></td><td>Crosses the blood-brain barrier; mobilizes tightly bound $Hg^{2+}, Pb^{2+}, Al^{3+}$ from neural organelles into the interstitial matrix.</td><td>Basal ganglia, hippocampus, mitochondrial cristae.</td></tr>\n        <tr><th scope=\"row\" data-accent=\"blue\">Tier 2: Extracellular &amp; Vascular Buffering</th><td><strong>Wild Garlic Tincture</strong> (-SH groups) + <strong>Sarsaparilla</strong></td><td>Active sulfhydryl groups bind mobilized ionic metals; saponins bind circulating LPS endotoxins in blood and lymph.</td><td>Capillary blood beds, systemic lymphatic circulation.</td></tr>\n        <tr><th scope=\"row\" data-accent=\"rose\">Tier 3: Hepatic Conjugation &amp; Biliary Transit</th><td><strong>Andrographis</strong> + <strong>TUDCA</strong> + <strong>Wormwood</strong></td><td>Stimulates Phase I/II hepatic glutathione conjugation; thins caustic bile and pumps neutralized toxins into the duodenum.</td><td>Hepatocytes, gallbladder, common bile duct.</td></tr>\n        <tr><th scope=\"row\" data-accent=\"violet\">Tier 4: Luminal Intestinal Trapping</th><td><strong>Broken-Cell Wall Chlorella</strong></td><td>Polysaccharide ion-exchange matrix irreversibly binds heavy metals and bile acids, preventing enterohepatic recirculation.</td><td>Duodenum, jejunum, ileum, fecal stool exit.</td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n  </div>"
