   "summary": "Pre-protocol priming architecture, weekly titration schedules, and 5/2 pulsing parameters.",
   "html": "<div class=\"card\" data-accent=\"rose\">\n    <h3 class=\"card-kicker\">5.0 The Starter Foundation &amp; Drainage Priming Phase</h3>\n    <p>Before launching full high-dose antimicrobial blends, a <strong>7–14 day priming foundation</strong> is deployed using the starter triad to open liver bile ducts, reduce ER stress, reinforce gut tight junctions, and elevate endogenous glutathione.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"card-grid cols-3\">\n    <div class=\"card\" data-accent=\"teal\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-kicker\">1. TUDCA (250–500 mg)</h4>\n      <p>Thins toxic bile sludge, activates the Bile Salt Export Pump (BSEP), and resolves endoplasmic reticulum (ER) stress in hepatocytes, preparing the liver for high-volume waste filtration.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"card\" data-accent=\"amber\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-kicker\">2. ND 5% Black Seed Oil (1–2 tsp)</h4>\n      <p>Thymoquinone activates the Nrf2 antioxidant pathway, suppresses intestinal mucosal inflammation, and upregulates **ZO-1 / occludin** proteins to seal leaky gut junctions.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"card\" data-accent=\"blue\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-kicker\">3. ND Andrographis Extract</h4>\n      <p>Initiates gentle baseline spirochetal suppression while stimulating Phase I/II liver enzymes and boosting endogenous cellular glutathione synthesis.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <h3 class=\"sub-head\">3-Week Master Protocol Titration Ramp-Up Curve</h3>\n  <div class=\"table-scroll\">\n    <table class=\"data\">\n      <thead><tr><th>Protocol Week</th><th>Dose Per Blend (Blends 1–4)</th><th>Coriander Drops</th><th>Chlorella Dosing</th><th>Operational Focus</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr><th scope=\"row\" data-accent=\"teal\">Week 1 (Titration Start)</th><td>0.5 mL (15 drops), 2× daily</td><td>0 drops (Withheld)</td><td>2,000 mg at bedtime</td><td>Establish GI tolerance; evaluate initial die-off buffer capacity.</td></tr>\n        <tr><th scope=\"row\" data-accent=\"blue\">Week 2 (Expansion)</th><td>1.0 mL (30 drops), 2× daily</td><td>2 drops daily (16:00)</td><td>3,000 mg at bedtime</td><td>Introduce gentle CNS metal mobilization; confirm binder capture.</td></tr>\n        <tr><th scope=\"row\" data-accent=\"violet\">Week 3 (Full Dosing)</th><td>1.0 – 2.0 mL, 3× daily</td><td>3 – 5 drops daily</td><td>4,000 – 5,000 mg bedtime</td><td>Full therapeutic eradication; sustained microvascular perfusion.</td></tr>\n        <tr><th scope=\"row\" data-accent=\"amber\">Maintenance (Weeks 4–16+)</th><td>1.5 – 2.5 mL, 3× daily</td><td>5 drops daily</td><td>5,000 mg bedtime</td><td>Continuous deep tissue clearing and collagen reconstruction.</td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"card\" data-accent=\"green\">\n    <h3 class=\"card-kicker\">5.1 The 5 Days ON / 2 Days OFF Pulsing Cadence</h3>\n    <p>Stealth pathogens adapt to constant static antimicrobial pressure by downregulating metabolic activity and forming temporary cysts. The protocol enforces a strict weekly pulse:</p>\n    <ul class=\"list\">\n      <li><strong>5 Days Active Eradication (Monday – Friday):</strong> Full administration of all four custom blends, standalone mobilizers, and foundationals.</li>\n      <li><strong>2 Days Rest &amp; Drainage (Saturday – Sunday):</strong> Cease all antimicrobial blends (Blends 1–4). Continue drinking warm <em>Cistus</em> tea, take bedtime Chlorella, maintain cellular hydration with electrolytes, and allow the liver and lymphatic systems to evacuate residual metabolic waste.</li>\n    </ul>\n  </div>"
